0275: display off in two vsync ticks (NegroniFramebuffer.cpp; after 0259)

The panel memory is mapped write-combined (NegroniSurface::kernelAddress,
kIOMapWriteCombineCache): a read of it is an uncached bus read. The 0251 fade
(7 ticks, each a read-modify-write pass over 1080x2412 pixels) took about 1 s
per tick on the vsync work loop: log 2026-10-26 "display off (fade 7055 ms)",
"late ticks 136" + "swaps/s 0" every second of it, backboardd spinning in
SwapWait (3861 calls/s), the UI frozen for 7 s on every screen-off, and a
wake during the fade landing in the middle of it.

Now tick 0 waits for the GPU copy, releases the surfaces, stops zero-copy and
writes black with 8-byte stores (logs "display off: black in N us"); tick 1
calls the backlight (DBV 0 + DCS sleep, 0258, logs "display off (fade N ms,
DCS sleep ok)" with N expected <= 25 ms); then the 100 ms slow tick as before.
A RequestPowerChange(1) in between resets fFadeStep and the next tick redraws.
Boot-args unchanged.

